@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il07-nouns`
IMPORT `il07-refusals`
IMPORT `ito66-nouns`
IMPORT `ito66-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito66-d-common-source`
IMPORT `ito66-a-separate-calculation`
IMPORT `ito66-b-property-income`
IMPORT `ito66-ab-taxable-income`
IMPORT `ito66-c-credit-points`

-- ===========================================================================
-- IL-07 adapter for row IL-02: Income Tax Ordinance s 66, separate calculation.
--
-- Imports this row's nouns and refusals and IL-02's modules, and no other row.
-- It builds IL-02's `Spouses in a tax year` from the household and hands it to
-- IL-02's rules. It exposes booleans, numbers and this row's own record.
--
-- THE COUPLE AS IL-02 SEES IT (input conventions, BRIEF.md "The household"):
-- * the earner's only income is the salary, one item of income from personal
--   exertion of the kind `from employment` (s 66(a)(1)), for the whole year;
-- * the spouse has no income (the pipeline declines otherwise, and so does this
--   adapter, rather than build a spouse whose income it does not know);
-- * no property income under s 66(b), and neither spouse claims under (b);
-- * no common source of income (s 66(d)): a salary from an employer is not
--   "a source of income of one spouse that depends on the other's";
-- * every child is a child of both spouses, so (4A) and (6), which reach only a
--   widowed partner's own children, add nothing; the widowed flags are FALSE;
-- * no child has income within s 66(a)(3).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `IL-07 adapter — row IL-02`

§§ `The household, as IL-02's spouses in a tax year`

GIVEN `is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Sex`
`IL-02: the sex` `is a woman` MEANS
    IF `is a woman` THEN `a woman` ELSE `a man`

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`IL-02: the earner as a spouse, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    `A spouse` WITH
        `sex`                                            IS `IL-02: the sex` (e's `the earner is a woman`)
        `income from personal exertion`                  IS LIST (`An item of income from personal exertion` WITH
            `kind`           IS `from employment`
            `taxable amount` IS 12 TIMES e's `the earner's monthly salary`
            `paid in respect of employment income for which the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation` IS FALSE
            `the spouse was entitled to a separate calculation, in the five years before the pension began, for the income by virtue of which it is paid` IS FALSE)
        `taxable income not from personal exertion`      IS 0
        `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage` IS 0
        `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`      IS 0
        `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion` IS c's `the earner claims a separate calculation of the tax on the earner's income from personal exertion`
        `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)` IS FALSE
        `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted` IS FALSE
        `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`        IS c's `the earner would be entitled to a credit point under section 37 of the Income Tax Ordinance`
    WHERE
        e MEANS h's `the earner`

GIVEN c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `A spouse`
`IL-02: the earner's spouse as a spouse, in` c MEANS
    IF   NOT (s's `the spouse's taxable income in the tax year` EQUALS 0)
    THEN `IL-07 composes a household with one earner; a spouse with taxable income is outside it`
    ELSE `A spouse` WITH
             `sex`                                            IS `IL-02: the sex` (s's `the spouse is a woman`)
             `income from personal exertion`                  IS EMPTY
             `taxable income not from personal exertion`      IS 0
             `taxable income from property owned one year before the marriage` IS 0
             `taxable income from property inherited during the marriage`      IS 0
             `claims a separate calculation of the tax on income from personal exertion` IS FALSE
             `claims a separate calculation of the tax on the property income in subsection (b)` IS FALSE
             `a widow or widower when the present marriage was contracted` IS FALSE
             `would be entitled to a credit point under section 37`        IS FALSE
    WHERE
        s MEANS c's `the earner's spouse`

-- s 40(b)(3), incorporated by s 66(c)(4)(a): "שנת לידה" is the tax year in which
-- the child was born; a tax year is a calendar year (IL-02 NOTES.md A4).
GIVEN k IS AN `IL-07 child`
GIVETH A `A child`
`IL-02: the household's child` k MEANS
    `A child` WITH
        `tax year of birth`                              IS DATE_YEAR (k's `the child's date of birth`)
        `a child of the registered spouse`               IS TRUE
        `a child of the spouse who is not the registered spouse` IS TRUE
        `the mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year` IS k's `the child's mother elects to count one birth-year credit point in the following tax year`
        `taxable income from a transparent company`      IS 0
        `taxable income from a real estate investment trust` IS 0
        `taxable income from interest`                   IS 0
        `taxable income from capital gain`               IS 0

GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `Spouses in a tax year`
`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    `Spouses in a tax year` WITH
        `tax year`                                       IS h's `the year of the month`
        `the registered spouse`                          IS IF c's `the earner is the registered spouse` THEN `earner's record` ELSE `other's record`
        `the spouse who is not the registered spouse`    IS IF c's `the earner is the registered spouse` THEN `other's record` ELSE `earner's record`
        `children`                                       IS map `IL-02: the household's child` (h's `the children of the household`)
        `common source of income`                        IS NOTHING
    WHERE
        `earner's record` MEANS `IL-02: the earner as a spouse, in` h `married as` c
        `other's record`  MEANS `IL-02: the earner's spouse as a spouse, in` c

GIVEN c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A `Which spouse`
`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c MEANS
    IF c's `the earner is the registered spouse` THEN `registered spouse` ELSE `spouse who is not the registered spouse`

§§ `Section 66(c) — whether it governs, and what it gives`

@ref ITO s 66(c) chapeau, (a)(1), (c)(1A) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`IL-02: section 66(c) governs the earner's calculation, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    `s 66(c) — governs the calculation of the` (`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c) `in` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c)

@ref ITO s 66(c) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-02 reports that section 66(c) does not govern the earner's calculation` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-02 reports that section 66(c) does not govern the earner's calculation"

@ref ITO s 66(c)(2), (4)-(6) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4); IL-02's tax-year gate (ito66-tax-years.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH AN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner`
`IL-02: the credit points section 66(c) gives the earner, in` h `married as` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 66(c) — the credit points it gives the` (`IL-02: which spouse the earner is, in` c) `in` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c)
    WHEN `section 66(c) does not govern the spouse's calculation`
        THEN `IL-02 reports that section 66(c) does not govern the earner's calculation`
    WHEN `in a separate calculation` cp
        THEN `IL-07 credit points section 66(c) gives the earner` WITH
                 `IL-02's half point under section 36A, by section 66(c)(4)` IS cp's `one half point under section 36A, by paragraph (4)`
                 `IL-02's half point under section 37, by section 66(c)(2)`  IS cp's `one half point under section 37, by paragraph (2)`
                 `IL-02's points for children, by section 66(c)(4) to (6)`  IS cp's `points for children, by paragraphs (4), (4A), (5) and (6)`

-- F13 of row IL-02: the children's credit is the lesser of their value and the
-- tax on the spouse's income from personal exertion.
@ref ITO s 66(c)(1A), (4), (5) (row IL-02, ito66-c-credit-points.l4; IL-02 fork F13)
GIVEN `the points for children` IS A NUMBER
      `the value`               IS A NUMBER
      `the tax`                 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-02: the credit for` `the points for children` `children's points at a value of` `the value` `, set against a tax on income from personal exertion of` `the tax` MEANS
    `s 66(c)(4)-(5) — the credit for children, set against the tax on income from personal exertion:` `the points for children` `,` `the value` `,` `the tax`

§§ `Subsections (a) and (b) — where the salary is assessed (a cross-check only)`

-- The pipeline takes the earner's taxable income to be the year's salary in every
-- case the capstone answers (NOTES.md fork K4). Where the earner is the spouse
-- who is not registered, IL-02 itself places that income in the separate
-- calculation, and the tests compare the two. Where the earner is the registered
-- spouse, IL-02 says s 65 governs and does not compute it (its assumption A3).
@ref ITO s 66(a), (b) (row IL-02, ito66-ab-taxable-income.l4)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`IL-02 reports that no separate calculation is made under section 66(a) for this couple` MEANS
    REFUSE "IL-02 reports that no separate calculation is made under section 66(a) for this couple"

@ref ITO s 66(a), (b) (row IL-02, ito66-ab-taxable-income.l4)
GIVEN h IS AN `IL-07 household in a month`
      c IS AN `IL-07 couple`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`IL-02: the taxable income in the separate calculation under section 66(a), in` h `married as` c MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 66(a)-(b) — the calculations, for` (`IL-02: the spouses in the tax year, in` h `married as` c)
    WHEN `a separate calculation is made under subsection (a)` `on the registered spouse` `in the separate calculation` `own (b)`
        THEN `in the separate calculation`
    OTHERWISE `IL-02 reports that no separate calculation is made under section 66(a) for this couple`
